  "energy_arc": "Mukhada 1 (bars 1-2): 80% — Aggressive, forward-charging thrash groove introducing the sitar hook.\nTakeover (bars 3-4): 88% — Heavier downpicked wall of rhythm guitar re-interpreting the mukhada.\nTaan Long (bars 5-6): 96% — Peak technical frenzy; sitar shredding high taans over relentless double-kick drumming.\nMukhada 2 (bars 7-8): 100% — Full ensemble drive accelerating into an explosive, razor-sharp hard stop on sam.",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Plan: Ground the piece firmly on Sa (S) with a relentless thrash gallop locked to Teentaal (16 beats). In Section 0 (mukhada), establish the head chord pattern following the harmony plan: 8 beats of S, 4 beats of r, 2 beats of m, and 2 beats of S resolving into sam. Section 1 is a takeover where guitar plays the mukhada theme directly, so by rule no part is written for it. In Section 2 (taan_long), lock into an unrelenting pedal on S with full driving double-kick thrash gallops under the sitar's rapid 16th taan lines. In Section 3 (final mukhada), repeat the head pattern from Section 0 (same_as: 0) culminating in a tight, razor-sharp hard stop on the climactic sam.",
